        "retained": [
          "Replace recursive binary quicksort with sampled three-splitter, four-bucket partitioning for large ranges.",
          "Count and scatter each worker's contiguous input chunk through OpenMP tasks, using per-worker bucket counts and disjoint scratch-array destinations.",
          "Create tasks for sufficiently large disjoint buckets while sorting smaller buckets locally; cap partition parallelism at four workers.",
          "Use duplicate-aware three-way introsort with insertion-sort and heapsort fallbacks for small or imbalanced ranges."
        ]
      },
      "hypothesis": "A sampled four-bucket partition with per-worker counts and disjoint scatter should expose coarse, independent sort ranges to four OpenMP workers with fewer recursive partition stages than binary task quicksort; an introsort fallback and size cutoffs preserve performance and correctness on skewed or duplicate-heavy inputs.",
